    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508-a2">

                <pb facs="0931" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg871"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Señor
                        Barrenechea.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 20, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Fearful that the interview of this morning
                    may have led to misconstruction from the natural imperfections of translation, I
                    beg leave to transmit herewith the correspondence which has passed between the
                    admiral and myself in relation to the matter in question.</p>
                <p>Nothing would give the admiral and his command more pleasure than to serve your
                    distressed countrymen in the hour of their great calamity. You will please
                    inform the admiral by one o’clock to-morrow how he can assist you, as his
                    vessel, the Powhatan, will sail about three p. m.</p>
                <p>I beg to assure, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. P. HOVEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Señor Dr. Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A.
                            Barrenechea,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
